---
import CaseStudy from '../layouts/CaseStudy.astro';

const facts = [
  { k: 'City', v: 'Barcelona' },
  { k: 'Year', v: '2021' },
  { k: 'Homes', v: '20' },
  { k: 'Architects', v: 'Lacol + LaBoqueria' },
  { k: 'Tenure', v: 'Cession of use' },
  { k: 'Land', v: 'Public lease, Poblenou' },
];

const gallery = [
  { placeholder: 'Galleries — photo needed', cap: 'Access galleries onto the shared side' },
  { placeholder: 'Common terrace — photo needed', cap: 'The communal terrace' },
  { placeholder: 'Street facade — photo needed', cap: 'Twenty homes on a public-land lease in Poblenou' },
];
---

<CaseStudy
  title="La Balma"
  subtitle="La Borda's sibling — proof the model repeats."
  heroPlaceholder="La Balma hero — gallery facade (photo needed)"
  facts={facts}
  gallery={gallery}
  prev={{ href: '/gleis-21/', label: 'Gleis 21' }}
>
  <section class="mx-auto max-w-[760px] px-6 pt-16 sm:px-12">
    <p class="text-[21px] leading-[1.62]">
      Three years after La Borda, the same tenure landed on a different lot: twenty homes in cession
      of use on public land in Poblenou, designed by Lacol with LaBoqueria, with the familiar
      grammar — access galleries, shared rooms, a communal terrace, modest private units backed by
      generous common ones.
    </p>
    <p class="mt-6 text-[21px] leading-[1.62]">
      What to steal: the repetition itself. La Balma is the evidence that La Borda was a model, not
      a miracle — same legal wrapper, same participatory process, second verse. That is the whole
      thesis of this site's Scale page.
    </p>
  </section>

  <Fragment slot="lessons">
    <li>
      The second building is cheaper than the first: the charter, lawyers, and lessons are already
      paid for.
    </li>
    <li>Cession of use survived contact with a second lot — the wrapper travels.</li>
    <li>Twenty homes is a viable co-op: don't wait for the perfect big parcel.</li>
    <li>Publish everything, as Lacol does — the next group starts at chapter two.</li>
  </Fragment>

  <Fragment slot="sources">
    Sources: <a href="https://www.lacol.coop" target="_blank" rel="noopener">lacol.coop</a>
  </Fragment>
</CaseStudy>
